<%# THE LIBRARY'S COLUMN (Shop manual spec §7), on every Library page: a folder, a file's page, the 3D
    models view, a model's page, Trash. Folders first, as a tree (spec §9; ShellHelper#column_tree,
    Maker::FolderTree): the library root, its folders, the chain down to the folder this page shows
    open with each level's siblings, and every folder the maker opened, which the `library_tree`
    cookie remembers across pages (column_tree_controller.js writes it, the server renders it into
    the first byte: design-system.md rule 7). Then the two other Library views as rows. The folder
    this page shows is the lit row; on a file's page that is the file's folder. %>
<div class="column-group" data-controller="column-tree">
  <h2 class="column-head">Folders</h2>
  <ul class="column-tree">
    <li class="column-tree-item">
      <%= column_row "Library", files_path, key: [ :library ] %>
      <%= folder_tree_level(column_tree.branches, parent_id: nil, depth: 1, more: column_tree.more?) %>
    </li>
  </ul>
</div>
<div class="column-group">
  <h2 class="column-head">Also</h2>
  <%= column_row "3D models", files_models_path, key: [ :models ] %>
  <%= column_row "Trash", trash_index_path, key: [ :trash ] %>
</div>
